WEBVTT

00:00:00.253 --> 00:00:03.592
Mia, imagine a whole cheese
and bean sandwich trying to

00:00:03.593 --> 00:00:05.614
squeeze into a tiny blood vessel.

00:00:05.994 --> 00:00:07.834
What is wrong with that delivery plan?

00:00:08.632 --> 00:00:09.248
Everything.

00:00:09.705 --> 00:00:13.684
The bread gets stuck, the cheese
complains, and my blood becomes lunch.

00:00:14.472 --> 00:00:15.259
Exactly.

00:00:15.581 --> 00:00:19.753
Food contains large molecules that
cannot simply cross the gut wall intact.

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:23.226
Digestion breaks them into smaller
molecules that can be absorbed.

00:00:23.549 --> 00:00:26.459
But first, what useful
things are in that lunch?

00:00:27.278 --> 00:00:30.599
Carbohydrates for energy,
protein for growth and repair,

00:00:30.855 --> 00:00:32.638
and fats for energy stores.

00:00:33.355 --> 00:00:33.756
Good.

00:00:34.169 --> 00:00:37.298
Our course groups a balanced
diet into seven categories:

00:00:37.561 --> 00:00:43.285
carbohydrates, proteins, fats,
vitamins, minerals, fiber, and water.

00:00:43.783 --> 00:00:46.967
Balanced means suitable
amounts and proportions, not

00:00:47.019 --> 00:00:48.706
equal piles of every food.

00:00:49.504 --> 00:00:54.230
So seven spoons of sugar and seven
spoons of water is not balanced

00:00:54.245 --> 00:00:55.693
just because the numbers match?

00:00:56.458 --> 00:00:57.440
Definitely not.

00:00:57.930 --> 00:01:01.039
Rice, bread, and potatoes
supply carbohydrate.

00:01:01.446 --> 00:01:04.964
Beans, lentils, eggs, and
dairy can supply protein.

00:01:05.423 --> 00:01:08.313
Oils, nuts, and cheese supply fats.

00:01:08.777 --> 00:01:11.951
Foods often contain several
nutrients, not just one.

00:01:12.742 --> 00:01:16.413
Vitamins and minerals are the tiny
ingredients with important jobs?

00:01:17.176 --> 00:01:17.734
Yes.

00:01:18.128 --> 00:01:20.667
Vitamin C supports
healthy connective tissue.

00:01:21.099 --> 00:01:25.585
Vitamin D helps us absorb calcium,
and calcium supports bones and teeth.

00:01:26.066 --> 00:01:29.063
Iron is needed for hemoglobin,
the oxygen-carrying

00:01:29.067 --> 00:01:30.770
substance in red blood cells.

00:01:31.533 --> 00:01:34.849
Fiber must be pointless if
our enzymes cannot digest it.

00:01:35.624 --> 00:01:38.143
My imaginary teacher
tear has arrived early.

00:01:38.709 --> 00:01:40.863
Fiber helps healthy bowel movement.

00:01:41.198 --> 00:01:43.742
Whole grains, fruit, and
vegetables supply it.

00:01:44.158 --> 00:01:48.114
Water is essential for transport and the
reactions happening throughout the body.

00:01:48.893 --> 00:01:50.905
So food is not only fuel,

00:01:51.499 --> 00:01:53.584
it also supplies materials and helps

00:01:53.585 --> 00:01:54.614
systems work.

00:01:55.355 --> 00:01:56.197
Exactly.

00:01:56.616 --> 00:01:59.738
A varied diet helps supply
the different things we need.

00:02:00.097 --> 00:02:03.911
We are learning their jobs, not
writing a personal diet prescription

00:02:04.095 --> 00:02:05.841
What is a deficiency disease?

00:02:06.701 --> 00:02:10.594
An illness caused by not getting enough
of a particular nutrient over time,

00:02:11.066 --> 00:02:12.863
not something you catch from a sneeze.

00:02:13.649 --> 00:02:14.195
Correct.

00:02:14.556 --> 00:02:18.059
Too little vitamin C can cause
scurvy, with problems such as

00:02:18.061 --> 00:02:20.258
bleeding gums and poor wound healing.

00:02:20.734 --> 00:02:24.859
Too little vitamin D or calcium
can contribute to rickets, with

00:02:24.859 --> 00:02:26.764
weak, soft bones in children.

00:02:27.493 --> 00:02:32.352
And not enough iron can cause anemia, so
the blood carries oxygen less effectively.

00:02:33.084 --> 00:02:33.700
Yes.

00:02:34.142 --> 00:02:38.063
Iron deficiency anemia involves
too little healthy hemoglobin.

00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:42.467
Anemia can have other causes too,
so these examples are not a way to

00:02:42.469 --> 00:02:44.324
diagnose yourself from one symptom.

00:02:45.169 --> 00:02:48.900
A missing ingredient can have a
specific effect, but does everyone

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:51.083
need the same amount of food energy?

00:02:51.847 --> 00:02:52.218
No.

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:57.658
Energy needs vary with body size, growth,
age, and activity, among other factors.

00:02:57.957 --> 00:03:01.716
A growing child and an adult doing
different amounts of activity will

00:03:01.717 --> 00:03:03.782
not necessarily need the same intake.

00:03:04.555 --> 00:03:07.205
If someone consistently takes
in more energy than they

00:03:07.205 --> 00:03:09.210
use, energy can be stored.

00:03:09.525 --> 00:03:11.902
If less, the body uses its stores.

00:03:12.669 --> 00:03:15.338
Right, but one meal tells us very little.

00:03:15.775 --> 00:03:18.745
We do not judge bodies or
compare classmates' food.

00:03:19.214 --> 00:03:22.393
The exam point is that needs
vary, and balanced intake

00:03:22.394 --> 00:03:23.756
supports health and growth.

00:03:24.557 --> 00:03:27.166
How do we know which
nutrients a food contains?

00:03:27.554 --> 00:03:28.510
Reading the label?

00:03:29.245 --> 00:03:33.355
That is useful, but a laboratory
can test for particular substances.

00:03:33.874 --> 00:03:36.777
Let's swap the lunch plate
for four labeled test tubes.

00:03:37.018 --> 00:03:40.085
No tasting anything once it
enters a science experiment

00:03:40.501 --> 00:03:42.804
First mystery sample: starch.

00:03:43.221 --> 00:03:44.498
What reagent goes in?

00:03:45.282 --> 00:03:46.476
Iodine solution.

00:03:46.902 --> 00:03:50.852
It starts orange-brown and turns
blue-black if starch is present.

00:03:51.559 --> 00:03:52.107
Correct.

00:03:52.379 --> 00:03:56.450
If it stays orange-brown, that is a
negative result under the test conditions.

00:03:56.937 --> 00:03:59.556
Next is a reducing sugar, such as glucose.

00:03:59.899 --> 00:04:02.337
We add Benedict's solution, then what?

00:04:03.126 --> 00:04:04.038
Look for orange.

00:04:04.605 --> 00:04:05.919
I might have skipped a step.

00:04:06.628 --> 00:04:09.737
Heat it in a water bath following
the teacher's procedure.

00:04:10.056 --> 00:04:12.600
Forgetting the heating
could lose the method mark.

00:04:13.018 --> 00:04:16.592
A positive result can range from
green through yellow and orange

00:04:16.831 --> 00:04:20.246
to a brick red precipitate,
depending on the amount present.

00:04:21.011 --> 00:04:23.058
No heating, incomplete method.

00:04:23.491 --> 00:04:25.927
The marking pen would not be impressed.

00:04:26.655 --> 00:04:28.050
Third, protein.

00:04:28.468 --> 00:04:32.618
Biuret reagent changes from blue
to purple or lilac with protein.

00:04:33.298 --> 00:04:34.652
Fourth, lipids.

00:04:35.177 --> 00:04:38.502
For the ethanol emulsion test,
mix the sample with ethanol,

00:04:38.599 --> 00:04:40.080
then add the extract to water.
